From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:31:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mgmt: hawkbit: report a reverted update as a failure

The action ID is saved before rebooting into the new image. If the
application does not confirm that image and MCUboot reverts it, the
previous image still finds the ID set on its next probe and reports the
action as finished successfully, so the server shows an update that is
not running.

Before reporting, check the running slot against the artifact's SHA-256
and report failure on a mismatch.

Signed-off-by: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
---
 subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c b/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c
index 6f7c65e4f..e94b8724a 100644
--- a/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c
+++ b/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ LOG_MODULE_REGISTER(hawkbit, CONFIG_HAWKBIT_LOG_LEVEL);
 
 #define HTTP_HEADER_CONTENT_TYPE_JSON "application/json;charset=UTF-8"
 
+#define SLOT0_LABEL slot0_partition
 #define SLOT1_LABEL slot1_partition
 #define SLOT1_SIZE  PARTITION_SIZE(SLOT1_LABEL)
 
@@ -1518,6 +1519,23 @@ static enum smf_state_result s_report(void *o)
 	};
 	uint8_t status_buffer[CONFIG_HAWKBIT_STATUS_BUFFER_SIZE] = {0};
 	char url_buffer[URL_BUFFER_SIZE] = {0};
+	struct flash_img_check fic = {.match = s->hb_context.dl.file_hash};
+
+	/* The action ID is saved before the reboot into the new image, so it is
+	 * also set when MCUboot reverted that image. Only report success if the
+	 * running slot holds the artifact.
+	 */
+	ret = hawkbit_parse_deployment(&s->hb_context, &s->hb_context.results.dep, NULL);
+	if (ret == 0) {
+		fic.clen = s->hb_context.dl.file_size;
+		ret = flash_img_check(&s->hb_context.flash_ctx, &fic, PARTITION_ID(SLOT0_LABEL));
+	}
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		LOG_ERR("Running image is not action %d's artifact (%d): update was reverted",
+			s->hb_context.json_action_id, ret);
+		feedback.status.result.finished =
+			hawkbit_status_finished(HAWKBIT_STATUS_FINISHED_FAILURE);
+	}
 
 	snprintk(url_buffer, sizeof(url_buffer), "%s/%s/%s/%d/%s", HAWKBIT_JSON_URL,
 		 s->device_id, "deploymentBase", s->hb_context.json_action_id, "feedback");
-- 
